    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0181" n="81" xml:id="pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5531/151a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-08T19:00:00-05:00">November 8, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Department’s 47, October 12, 7 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d77-f1"/> It has
                    been decided that the American memorandum of desiderata will be given to the
                    Belgian Chargé on Monday, November 12, at 11 a.m. We have now arranged that
                    Belgian officials in Brussels will on the same day hand you the Belgian
                    memorandum of desiderata. It will not be handed to the Department at the same
                    time by de Ligne. Please telegraph in brief form a list of the concessions which
                    Belgium will ask<anchor n="15" xml:id="d77-f2"/> and forward the full memorandum
                    by mail at the earliest possible moment. Our memorandum of desiderata will be
                    sent to you by the earliest pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
